 ```
 python3 primus_turbo/hipkittens/gfx1250_mla_fwd/gen/build.py --out OUT [--sched list|program] [--asmkit-root DIR]
+    [--diag] [--csgpr] [--qgroup none|pair|late] [--worder TAGS] [--trans-cost N]
 ```
 
+The shipped candidates (W-S1a2) are built with
+`--csgpr --qgroup late --worder QK0,QK1,PV0,QK2,QK3,PV1,PV2,PV3 --trans-cost 3` (and `--diag` for the diagonal-tile
+variant). All of these only change the instruction schedule / operand form, never the math (bit-identical by design,
+checked by `tools/emu.py`):
+
+- `--csgpr`: the shell passes `c2 = scale * log2(e)` to every TILE marker (`-DHKGEN_TILE_C2=1`); the tile copies it
+  into `s[102:103]` and the packed `p = fma(s, c, -m')` reads it as a scalar pair (`op_sel_hi` 0: both halves read
+  s102). A `v_pk_fma_f32` with 3 VGPR sources costs ~0.75 cycle more (fwd measurement J5); the mask rotation shrinks
+  to s99..s101.
+- `--qgroup late` + `--worder`: the Q re-reads of q tiles 2 / 3 overwrite the buffers QK(0) / QK(1) read; under the
+  expert-mode rule LLVM uses (`va_vdst(0)` once more than one VALU class is in flight) each re-read that follows its
+  buffer's last WMMA reader needs a full drain. All 24 re-reads are issued after the last QK(1) WMMA (one drain per
+  tile instead of five) and the WMMA stream runs `QK0 QK1 PV0 QK2 QK3 PV1 PV2 PV3`, so PV(0) hides the LDS latency
+  of the re-reads.
+- `--trans-cost`: the list scheduler's issue cost of a TRANS op (model parameter only).
+
 1. `amdclang++ -x hip --offload-arch=gfx1250 --cuda-device-only --no-gpu-bundle-output -O3 -std=c++20 -DNDEBUG -I.
    -save-temps=obj -mllvm -amdgpu-expert-scheduling-mode -cuid=k_mla_fwd -DHKGEN_REF=0 -c hip/k_mla_fwd.hip`
    (cwd `hip/`); the saved `.s` is `OUT/shell.s`. The same with `-DHKGEN_REF=1` gives `OUT/ref/k_mla_fwd.hsaco`
